        "text": "Voting is a legitimate and effective means of enacting change on issues of systemic racism.",
        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "Protest movements and electoral politics represent distinct but potentially complementary strategies for social change.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "The speaker believes that both protest and political engagement have value, even if they are perceived as conflicting.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "Audiences understand the context of current protests against police violence and systemic racism.",
        "confidence": 0.89
      },
      {
        "text": "It is reasonable to expect individuals to engage with multiple forms of activism simultaneously.",
