    "turn_text": "sitting at the capital and anti-bacuate. So believe you me, it was heavy duty. And the people who died and who now are ill and have disabilities as a result of that. That's what stays on my mind. So that was the hard part. People suffering and dying is a result of these terrible attacks. And for me, you know, as a person of faith, I have to say my prayers and just do it and stand. You know, there's a scripture in Ephesians that you just stand. I mean, I paraphrase and I, when all hell breaks out around you and you put on the full armor of God and you just stand, well, that's what I had to do. And I knew one of these days, if I kept being persistent, my dad was in the military, first person called me, he said, that was the right vote. Do not send our troops in hard way unless you know what the heck you're doing, what the exit strategy, where they're going. I mean, if you read that 61, authorization, it was so broad, it's crazy.",
