    "turn_text": "so the thing is, the right to descent is central to our democracy. Whether you agree or not, people have that right and should if they think their government is not doing the right thing. But to me, when I saw it, there was 60,000 emails and there are Mills College now and phone calls and letters. So I have them archived if anyone wants to see them, you can go to Mills. But you know what, on the other hand, there was so many like from Bishop Tutu and Paretta Scott King, people from all around the world who sent me notes and told me that was the right vote, that they stood with me, just don't back down. And so that was, on the other hand, so many people whose names, who I will never meet. And then another woman, while she was right outside of my district, She wrote me a letter and she said, you know, I hated you. I was one of those that called you all kinds of names and boom, boom, boom. And she said, look, it's not a lot, but I'm sitting you a check for $15. She said, because now I understand that I have kids and this has been going on for 20 years and this. You know, so she just went on and I",
